      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Phyllotaxis sets seed after seed a fixed Angle round from the last, as a sunflower does; at the golden angle, 0.382 of a turn, they pack without gaps. An Oscillator rocks the Angle a hair either side, and the seeds swirl into spiral arms. Its Background is a Spiral, turned by the Master Gear. Try Count and Dot Size."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
